title: War Aims
card-image: img/cards/foreign_policy.svg?v=2
subtitle: Peace without annexations, the Stockholm conference and the offensive.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: coalition_affairs
view-if: foreign_policy_timer <= 0 and at_war = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; foreign_policy_timer = 3

The Allies want the offensive. The soldiers want peace. The Soviet's formula is peace without annexations or indemnities, but nobody has agreed to negotiate on it.

- @note: Send a new note to the Allies on war aims.
- @stockholm: Back the Stockholm conference of the International.
- @offensive: Prepare the offensive with the Allies.
- @separate: Sound out Germany through neutral intermediaries.
- @easy_discard

@note

How should it be carried out? Phased in, with compensation and negotiation, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. By decree it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can pass it and enforce it against them.

- @note_slow: Phase it in, with compensation and negotiation.
- @note_decree: Pass it by decree, as written.
- @note_force: Pass it by decree, and break any opposition by force.

@note_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -2, rel_kad: -2});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 2, workers: 1});
Q.war_aims_note = 1;
});
!}

A note on war aims went to London and Paris. They replied politely, and not at all. It was phased in slowly, with compensation where it was owed, and the opposition grumbled rather than raged.



@note_decree
subtitle: The law as written. Its opponents will answer.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'decree', () => {
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -2, rel_kad: -2});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 2, workers: 1});
Q.war_aims_note = 1;
});
!}

A note on war aims went to London and Paris. They replied politely, and not at all.



@note_force
choose-if: strength >= 18
subtitle: Chance of breaking its opponents: Kadets [+ odds_kad +]%. A camp under 45% is too strong to touch, and is left alone.
unavailable-subtitle: We lack the force and the allies to break the opposition.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'force', () => {
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -2, rel_kad: -2});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 2, workers: 1});
Q.war_aims_note = 1;
});
!}

A note on war aims went to London and Paris. They replied politely, and not at all. [+ law_text +]

@stockholm

How should it be carried out? Phased in, with compensation and negotiation, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. By decree it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can pass it and enforce it against them.

- @stockholm_slow: Phase it in, with compensation and negotiation.
- @stockholm_decree: Pass it by decree, as written.
- @stockholm_force: Pass it by decree, and break any opposition by force.

@stockholm_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
Q.stockholm = (Q.stockholm || 0) + 1;
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -4, rel_kad: -4, army_discipline: -1});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 3, workers: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 4);
});
!}

The government has officially endorsed a socialist conference at Stockholm. The Allied governments refuse passports to their own socialists. [? if stockholm >= 3 : Delegates from four neutral and enemy countries are on their way. ?] It was phased in slowly, with compensation where it was owed, and the opposition grumbled rather than raged.



