@offensive
on-arrival: {!
Q.offensive_prepared = 1;
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: 3, army_discipline: 3, rel_kad: 4});
RO.boost(Q, {middle: 3, soldiers: -3});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 4);
!}

Kerensky is visiting the front, and the Soviet has given its blessing. The army is getting ready for an offensive that it does not want.

@separate
choose-if: stockholm >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: We must first have shown our commitment to a general peace at Stockholm.

How should it be carried out? Phased in, with compensation and negotiation, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. By decree it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can pass it and enforce it against them.

- @separate_slow: Phase it in, with compensation and negotiation.
- @separate_decree: Pass it by decree, as written.
- @separate_force: Pass it by decree, and break any opposition by force.

@separate_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
Q.separate_feelers = 1;
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -6, rel_kad: -6, right_threat: 3});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', -2, 6);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, -1);
});
!}

An unofficial approach, through a Swedish socialist, asked if Germany would consider terms on the basis of no annexations. The answer was not hostile. The Kadets learned of it and are furious. It was phased in slowly, with compensation where it was owed, and the opposition grumbled rather than raged.



